{"author":{"id":"8022379585b4ab99ca8775db3eb67d33fcb256817114c28e51ccc1e9f55cdec4"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1789843131,"nonce":"ZjLj2i4HtzJoYmPLYqx53DrqTSM=","title":"Xml.parse throws an object that prints as a pointer; the XML tests now reach it","message":"With the E0801 tag switch no longer carrying SIMD arms, `haxe.xml.Parser.doParse` compiles on every backend, and Issue11883 / Issue4094 / Issue4096 / TestXML run into `Uncaught exception: 12888047680` at `Xml.parse(\"\u003cfoo\u003exx\u003c/foo\u003e bar\u0026lt;\")` -- exit 1, which the harness files as COMPILE_FAIL.\n\nTwo things: the parser throws where Haxe's does not (an `escapes.get` still goes through the E0801 runtime switch with an unresolved receiver, so the first entity lookup throws), and the uncaught-exception report prints a thrown object's address instead of its `toString` (the `TO_STRING_REGISTRY` from cc70fe31 has it).","files":null}]}